# NEER – Hardware Components

## Overview

This document lists the hardware components used in the NEER floating water waste collection robot and explains their functions.

| Component | Function | Specifications to Record |
|---|---|---|
| ESP32 | Main controller | Board model, operating voltage |
| Geared DC motors | Propulsion | Rated voltage, RPM, torque |
| Motor driver | Motor direction control | Model, voltage and current rating |
| Relay module | Electrical switching | Channel count, coil voltage |
| Collection motor | Drives collection assembly | Voltage, RPM, current |
| Lithium-ion battery | Power supply | Cell configuration, capacity |
| Voltage regulator | Voltage regulation | Input and output voltage |
| Mesh fabric | Waste collection | Material and dimensions |
| Rollers | Conveyor movement | Diameter and dimensions |
| PVC pipes | Structural support | Diameter and length |
| Floats | Buoyancy | Dimensions and quantity |
| Collection tray | Waste storage | Dimensions and capacity |
| Waterproof enclosure | Electronics protection | Material and dimensions |

## Component Selection Considerations

Components were identified based on affordability, accessibility, weight, compatibility and suitability for a small floating robotic platform.

Exact specifications and quantities must be filled in using the final assembled prototype.

## Electrical Safety

- Verify voltage compatibility before connecting components.
- Avoid powering motors directly from ESP32 GPIO pins.
- Use suitable motor drivers for inductive motor loads.
- Provide appropriate current protection.
- Protect all electrical connections from water exposure.
- Verify the battery configuration and charging requirements.
